@startuml candidate-session-state
title Candidate Consumer Session Lifecycle (Pre-CP2A)

skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam stateArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

[*] --> NO_SESSION : instance starts as follower

NO_SESSION --> JOINING : leader.tryAcquire() succeeds\nrunLeaderSession() begins

JOINING --> ACTIVE : startCandidateConsumerSession()\nconnect + subscribe + run resolve

ACTIVE --> LEAVING : lease lost (renewal Lua returns 0)\nOR SIGTERM/shutdown()

LEAVING --> NO_SESSION : session.stop() -> consumer.disconnect()\n(memoized -- safe from any caller)

note right of ACTIVE
  Scan loop runs concurrently.
  activeSession / activeSessionAbort
  are set at module scope so shutdown()
  can reach this term's session.
end note

note right of LEAVING
  stop() is idempotent: the lease-loss
  callback, this session's own teardown,
  and shutdown() may all call it without
  coordinating who goes first -- every
  caller converges on the same disconnect()
  promise, never a second one.
end note

note bottom of NO_SESSION
  A follower never enters JOINING.
  Only a lease acquisition attempt
  can start this lifecycle.
end note

@enduml
